                        <field name="dc_description">This manuscript, probably written in Italy in the second quarter of the 15th century, contains the canonist Wilhelm Horborch’s († 1384) collection of judicial decisions of the Rota Romana. The manuscript probably reached the library of the monastery of St. Gall along with other codices from the estate of St. Gall Abbott Kaspar von Breitenlandenberg (1442–1463), who had studied canon law in Bologna from 1439 until 1442 under Johannes de Anania. </field>
